traces.inference_trace:
The minimum number of operations equals the sum of the prime factors of n, counted with multiplicity. For n = 1 the sum is 0.

To compute it, divide out each factor d starting from 2: while d divides n, add d to the answer and set n = n / d. Then move to the next d.

The starter snippet declares `var minSteps = function(n)` rather than a class, so I keep that shape.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {number} n
 * @return {number}
 */
var minSteps = function(n) {
    let ans = 0;
    for (let d = 2; d * d <= n; d++) {
        while (n % d === 0) {
            ans += d;
            n = n / d;
        }
    }
    if (n > 1) ans += n;
    return ans;
};
```

