traces.inference_trace:
Scan the array once and remember the index of the previous 1. When the next 1 appears at index `i`, there are `i - prev - 1` zeros between the two. If that count is less than `k`, return false. If the scan finishes without a violation, return true.

The starter snippet is a function expression (`var kLengthApart = function(nums, k)`), so I keep that form.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {number[]} nums
 * @param {number} k
 * @return {boolean}
 */
var kLengthApart = function(nums, k) {
    let prev = -1;
    for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
        if (nums[i] === 1) {
            if (prev !== -1 && i - prev - 1 < k) return false;
            prev = i;
        }
    }
    return true;
};
```

