This is solved with a union-find that processes the hits in reverse.

1. Copy the grid and remove every brick that will be hit. Only cells that actually held a brick (value 1) are marked, so hits on empty cells are handled correctly.
2. Build a union-find over the remaining bricks. Use a virtual root node at index m*n for the top of the grid, and keep a size count at each root. Union every brick in row 0 with the virtual root.
3. Process the hits in reverse. For hit i at (r, c):
   - If the original cell was 0, the answer is 0.
   - Otherwise record the current size of the top component, restore the brick, and union it with the top if r == 0 and with each adjacent brick.
   - The new top size minus the old top size, minus 1 for the restored brick itself, is the number of bricks that fell. Clamp this at 0.

Since all hit coordinates are unique, restoring bricks in reverse order is safe.

Implementation notes: the union-find uses an iterative `find` with path compression, and `size` is an array. The virtual root's size starts at 1, which is fine because only differences are used.

```javascript
var hitBricks = function(grid, hits) {
    const m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;
    const g = grid.map(r => r.slice());
    for (const [r, c] of hits) {
        if (g[r][c] === 1) g[r][c] = 2;
    }
    const top = m * n;
    const parent = new Int32Array(m * n + 1);
    const size = new Int32Array(m * n + 1).fill(1);
    for (let i = 0; i <= m * n; i++) parent[i] = i;
    const find = (x) => {
        while (parent[x] !== x) {
            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]];
            x = parent[x];
        }
        return x;
    };
    const union = (a, b) => {
        a = find(a); b = find(b);
        if (a === b) return;
        if (size[a] < size[b]) { const t = a; a = b; b = t; }
        parent[b] = a;
        size[a] += size[b];
    };
    const dirs = [[1, 0], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [0, -1]];
    for (let r = 0; r < m; r++) {
        for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {
            if (g[r][c] !== 1) continue;
            if (r === 0) union(r * n + c, top);
            if (r > 0 && g[r - 1][c] === 1) union(r * n + c, (r - 1) * n + c);
            if (c > 0 && g[r][c - 1] === 1) union(r * n + c, r * n + c - 1);
        }
    }
    const res = new Array(hits.length).fill(0);
    for (let i = hits.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        const [r, c] = hits[i];
        if (g[r][c] !== 2) continue;
        const before = size[find(top)];
        g[r][c] = 1;
        if (r === 0) union(r * n + c, top);
        for (const [dr, dc] of dirs) {
            const nr = r + dr, nc = c + dc;
            if (nr < 0 || nc < 0 || nr >= m || nc >= n) continue;
            if (g[nr][nc] === 1) union(r * n + c, nr * n + nc);
        }
        const after = size[find(top)];
        res[i] = Math.max(0, after - before - 1);
    }
    return res;
};
```

