The solution uses a lazy increment array. Each position `i` has an increment `inc[i]` that applies to element `i` and everything below it.

- **push:** if the stack has room, append `x` and set its increment to 0.
- **increment(k, val):** let `i = min(k, size) - 1`. If `i >= 0`, add `val` to `inc[i]`.
- **pop:** if the stack is empty, return -1. Otherwise let `i = size - 1`, and the result is `stack[i] + inc[i]`. If `i > 0`, pass `inc[i]` down with `inc[i-1] += inc[i]`. Then reset `inc[i] = 0` and shrink the stack.

The method is named `increment` in the starter code, so I keep that name. Every operation is O(1).

```javascript
var CustomStack = function(maxSize) {
    this.max = maxSize;
    this.stack = [];
    this.inc = [];
};

CustomStack.prototype.push = function(x) {
    if (this.stack.length < this.max) {
        this.stack.push(x);
        this.inc.push(0);
    }
};

CustomStack.prototype.pop = function() {
    if (this.stack.length === 0) return -1;
    const i = this.stack.length - 1;
    const res = this.stack[i] + this.inc[i];
    if (i > 0) this.inc[i - 1] += this.inc[i];
    this.stack.pop();
    this.inc.pop();
    return res;
};

CustomStack.prototype.increment = function(k, val) {
    const i = Math.min(k, this.stack.length) - 1;
    if (i >= 0) this.inc[i] += val;
};
```

