Split each cell into 4 triangles (0=top, 1=right, 2=bottom, 3=left) and merge them with union-find.

Within a cell:
- `' '` merges all four triangles.
- `'/'` merges top with left (0 and 3) and right with bottom (1 and 2).
- `'\'` merges top with right (0 and 1) and bottom with left (2 and 3).

Across cells:
- The bottom triangle (2) of cell (i,j) merges with the top triangle (0) of cell (i+1,j).
- The right triangle (1) of cell (i,j) merges with the left triangle (3) of cell (i,j+1).

The answer is the number of distinct components. The starter shape is a function expression, so I keep it as given. The index of triangle k in cell (i,j) is (i*n+j)*4+k.

```javascript
/**
 * @param {string[]} grid
 * @return {number}
 */
var regionsBySlashes = function(grid) {
    const n = grid.length;
    const p = new Array(n * n * 4);
    for (let i = 0; i < p.length; i++) p[i] = i;
    let count = p.length;
    const find = (x) => {
        while (p[x] !== x) {
            p[x] = p[p[x]];
            x = p[x];
        }
        return x;
    };
    const union = (a, b) => {
        a = find(a);
        b = find(b);
        if (a !== b) {
            p[a] = b;
            count--;
        }
    };
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            const base = (i * n + j) * 4;
            const c = grid[i][j];
            if (c === ' ') {
                union(base, base + 1);
                union(base + 1, base + 2);
                union(base + 2, base + 3);
            } else if (c === '/') {
                union(base, base + 3);
                union(base + 1, base + 2);
            } else {
                union(base, base + 1);
                union(base + 2, base + 3);
