Since values are at most 50, I keep for each value a stack of (node, depth) entries for the ancestors currently on the DFS path. For a node, I check every value v from 1 to 50 that is coprime with nums[node] and take the entry with the greatest depth among the tops of those stacks.

The DFS must be iterative, because n can be 1e5 and recursion could overflow the stack.

Implementation:
- Precompute `cop[a][b]` as whether gcd(a, b) == 1 for a, b in 1..50.
- Build the adjacency list.
- Use an explicit stack with an iterator index per node. On entering a node:
  - Compute its answer from the stacks of the coprime values.
  - Push (node, depth) onto the stack for nums[node].
- On exit, pop from the stack for nums[node].
- Each value's stack is an array of nodes. Depth is stored in a separate array.

Iterative flow:
- `stack = [0]`, `parent[0] = -1`, `idx[node]` is the pointer into the adjacency list, and `entered` is handled by processing the entry when the node is first pushed.
- Push a node: compute ans, push onto `st[nums[node]]`, set depth.
- Loop: take the top node u. If `idx[u] < adj[u].length`, take neighbor w; if w != parent[u], set parent[w] = u, depth[w] = depth[u]+1, process entry of w and push w. Otherwise, pop the DFS stack and pop `st[nums[u]]`.

For the answer on entry: best = -1, bestDepth = -1; for v in 1..50, if cop[nums[u]][v] and st[v] is nonempty, let t = the top of st[v]; if depth[t] > bestDepth, update. The root has no ancestors, so every stack is empty and the answer is -1. Note that nums[u] = 1 is coprime with 1 and with everything, which the gcd table handles.

```javascript
var getCoprimes = function(nums, edges) {
    const n = nums.length;
    const gcd = (a, b) => b === 0 ? a : gcd(b, a % b);
    const cop = [];
    for (let a = 0; a <= 50; a++) {
        cop.push(new Array(51).fill(false));
        for (let b = 1; b <= 50; b++) {
            if (a >= 1 && gcd(a, b) === 1) cop[a][b] = true;
        }
    }
    const adj = Array.from({length: n}, () => []);
    for (const [u, v] of edges) {
        adj[u].push(v);
        adj[v].push(u);
    }
    const ans = new Array(n).fill(-1);
    const depth = new Array(n).fill(0);
    const parent = new Array(n).fill(-1);
    const idx = new Array(n).fill(0);
    const st = [];
    for (let i = 0; i <= 50; i++) st.push([]);

    const enter = (u) => {
        let best = -1, bd = -1;
        const c = cop[nums[u]];
        for (let v = 1; v <= 50; v++) {
            if (c[v]) {
                const s = st[v];
                if (s.length > 0) {
                    const t = s[s.length - 1];
                    if (depth[t] > bd) {
                        bd = depth[t];
                        best = t;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        ans[u] = best;
        st[nums[u]].push(u);
    };

    const stack = [0];
    enter(0);
    while (stack.length > 0) {
        const u = stack[stack.length - 1];
        if (idx[u] < adj[u].length) {
            const w = adj[u][idx[u]++];
            if (w !== parent[u]) {
                parent[w] = u;
                depth[w] = depth[u] + 1;
                enter(w);
                stack.push(w);
            }
        } else {
            stack.pop();
            st[nums[u]].pop();
        }
    }
    return ans;
};
```

